y in Africa</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2005</year><volume>331</volume><fpage>780</fpage><lpage>781</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16195308</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.331.7519.780-b</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dumont</surname><given-names>J-C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lema&#x000ee;tre</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><source>Counting Immigrants and Expatriates in OECD Countries: A New Perspective</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Paris: Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pond</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>McPake</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The health migration crisis: the role of four Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development countries</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2006</year><volume>367</volume><fpage>1448</fpage><lpage>1455</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16650654</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(06)68346-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lopez</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mathers</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Ezzati</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jamison</surname><given-names>DT</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>CJL</given-names></name></person-group><source>Global Burden of Disease and Risk Factors</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>New York: Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Or